---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Personal Data & Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy and personal data protection for Domaine d'Aubigny. GDPR compliance, data rights, cookies and confidentiality information." lang="en">
  <style>
    .legal { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(56px, 12vw, 96px) var(--pad-x); }
    .legal__title { font-size: 36px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 48px; }
    .legal h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 500; margin: 32px 0 16px; }
    .legal h3 { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500; margin: 20px 0 12px; }
    .legal p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--body); margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .legal ul { margin-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .legal li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  </style>

  <section class="legal">
    <h1 class="legal__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Domaine d'Aubigny</strong> — Last updated: October 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
    <p>The data controller is <strong>Domaine d'Aubigny</strong>, a simplified joint-stock company with registered office at Hameau d'Aubigny, 71510 Aluze, France. Contact: contact@aubigny.wine | +33 3 85 44 76 76</p>

    <h2>2. Data Collection</h2>
    <p>Domaine d'Aubigny collects the following personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Order data:</strong> Name, first name, address, email, phone number, billing and delivery addresses</li>
      <li><strong>Payment data:</strong> Bank card information, processed exclusively by a secure payment provider (not retained by the Estate)</li>
      <li><strong>Contact data:</strong> Email, phone, messages sent via contact form</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> Anonymous browsing data via Plausible Analytics</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Purpose of Processing</h2>
    <p>Your personal data is used for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Processing and managing your orders</li>
      <li>Shipping your parcels</li>
      <li>Contacting you about your order or questions</li>
      <li>Improving service quality and the website</li>
      <li>Analyzing site usage in an anonymous manner</li>
      <li>Complying with legal obligations (tax, accounting)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
    <p>Data processing is based on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contract performance:</strong> For order management and delivery</li>
      <li><strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> To improve service and analyze site usage</li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> For tax and accounting purposes</li>
      <li><strong>Consent:</strong> For any newsletter distribution (optional)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>Order data is retained for 5 years from the end of the calendar year following the order, in compliance with tax and accounting obligations. Contact data is deleted after processing your request, unless you have consented to receive Estate communications. Payment data is not retained by Domaine d'Aubigny (managed entirely by an external provider).</p>

    <h2>6. Data Recipients</h2>
    <p>Your personal data is shared only with those necessary to process your order:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Licensed shipping carrier (for delivery)</li>
      <li>Secure payment provider</li>
      <li>Estate accountant and tax advisor (for accounting)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No data is sold or transferred to third parties for commercial purposes.</p>

    <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Under GDPR regulations, you have the following rights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Right of access:</strong> Access your personal data</li>
      <li><strong>Right of rectification:</strong> Correct inaccurate data</li>
      <li><strong>Right of erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your data</li>
      <li><strong>Right to restrict:</strong> Limit processing of your data</li>
      <li><strong>Right to portability:</strong> Receive your data in a structured format</li>
      <li><strong>Right to object:</strong> Object to data processing</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise these rights, write to contact@aubigny.wine with your request and a copy of your identification.</p>

    <h2>8. Data Security</h2>
    <p>Domaine d'Aubigny implements appropriate security measures to protect your data from unauthorized access, alteration, or destruction. Bank card payments are secured by a certified provider (SSL/TLS encryption).</p>

    <h2>9. Cookies & Trackers</h2>
    <p>The website uses <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong>, a privacy-friendly statistical analysis tool that does not use cookies. No specific consent is required for this analysis. The site does not deposit advertising or third-party tracking cookies.</p>

    <h2>10. Policy Changes</h2>
    <p>Domaine d'Aubigny reserves the right to modify this privacy policy. Any significant modifications will be notified to you.</p>

    <h2>11. Complaint</h2>
    <p>If you believe the processing of your data violates your rights, you may file a complaint with the <strong>Commission Nationale de l'Informatique et des Libertés (CNIL)</strong>: www.cnil.fr</p>
  </section>
</Base>
